## 🔄 The Complete Data Flow — Step by Step

This is the heart of the project. Here's exactly what happens when you run `npx tsx src/ingest.ts`:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["📄 party_master.xls"] -->|"fs.readFileSync + XLSX.read"| B["Raw Party Rows (array of objects)"]
    B -->|"mapPartyMasterRow()"| C["BusinessEntity[] — Clean typed objects"]
    
    D["📄 outstanding_legder.xls"] -->|"fs.readFileSync + XLSX.read"| E["Raw Outstanding Rows"]
    
    E -->|"Loop: for each row"| F{"resolveBusiness()"}
    C -->|"passed as lookup list"| F
    
    F -->|"FOUND"| G["Enrich: set currentOutstanding + computeRiskLevel()"]
    F -->|"AMBIGUOUS"| H["Skip — multiple matches"]
    F -->|"NOT_FOUND"| I["Skip — no match"]
    
    G -->|"saveBusiness()"| J["💾 SQLite: data/cdp.db"]
    
    K["🔍 view.ts"] -->|"SQL: SELECT WHERE LIKE"| J
```

### Phase-by-Phase Walkthrough:

#### Phase 1: Parse Party Master → BusinessEntity[]
```
party_master.xls  →  XLSX.read()  →  sheet_to_json()  →  mapPartyMasterRow()  →  BusinessEntity[]
```
Every row from the "Party Master" Excel sheet gets converted into a typed `BusinessEntity` object with a **canonical ID** (based on GSTIN > PAN > fallback name).

#### Phase 2: Parse Outstanding Ledger
```
outstanding_legder.xls  →  XLSX.read()  →  sheet_to_json()  →  raw row objects
```
Every row from the "Outstanding Ledger" is read as-is. Each row has a `Description` (business name) and `Total` (amount owed).

#### Phase 3: Identity Resolution + Enrichment + Save
```
For each outstanding row:
  1. resolveBusiness()  →  match it to a BusinessEntity using GSTIN or ledger name
  2. computeRiskLevel() →  assign LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH/CRITICAL based on amount
  3. saveBusiness()     →  INSERT or UPDATE in SQLite
```

