### 8. [`src/pipeline/ageing.ts`](file:///c:/Users/ASUS/my-agentic-cdp/src/pipeline/ageing.ts) — Risk Scoring Pipeline

```typescript
export function computeRiskLevel(currentOutstanding: number | undefined): RiskLevel | undefined {
    if (currentOutstanding === undefined) return undefined;   // No data = no risk score
    if (currentOutstanding > 250000) return 'CRITICAL';       // > ₹2.5 lakh
    if (currentOutstanding > 107000) return 'HIGH';           // > ₹1.07 lakh
    if (currentOutstanding > 29000)  return 'MEDIUM';         // > ₹29,000
    return 'LOW';                                             // ≤ ₹29,000
}
```

**Risk Tier Breakdown**:

| Outstanding Amount (₹) | Risk Level | Business Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| ≤ 29,000 | `LOW` | Normal, healthy debt |
| 29,001 – 107,000 | `MEDIUM` | Needs monitoring |
| 107,001 – 250,000 | `HIGH` | Serious overdue concern |
| > 250,000 | `CRITICAL` | Severe — needs immediate action |

**Key Learning**: This is called **"ageing"** in accounting. Real-world ageing analysis looks at how long invoices have been unpaid (30/60/90/120+ days). This simplified version uses amount thresholds instead of time, but the concept is the same — classify risk to prioritize collection efforts.

