### 9. [`src/db/database.ts`](file:///c:/Users/ASUS/my-agentic-cdp/src/db/database.ts) — Database Layer

```typescript
import Database from 'better-sqlite3';

// 1. Open (or create) the SQLite database file
const db = new Database('data/cdp.db');

// 2. Create the table schema (idempotent — safe to run multiple times)
db.exec(`
  CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS businesses (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,           -- Canonical ID: "gst:xxx" or "pan:xxx" or "party:xxx"
    name TEXT NOT NULL,            -- Business display name
    ledgerName TEXT NOT NULL,      -- Ledger/accounting name
    taxId TEXT,                    -- GSTIN (nullable)
    currentOutstanding REAL,       -- Amount owed (nullable, REAL = floating point)
    riskLevel TEXT                 -- "LOW" / "MEDIUM" / "HIGH" / "CRITICAL"
  )
`);
```

#### `saveBusiness()` — Upsert (Insert or Update)

```typescript
export function saveBusiness(business: BusinessEntity) {
  const stmt = db.prepare(`
    INSERT INTO businesses (id, name, ledgerName, taxId, currentOutstanding, riskLevel)
    VALUES (@id, @name, @ledgerName, @taxId, @currentOutstanding, @riskLevel)
    ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET
      name = @name,
      ledgerName = @ledgerName,
      taxId = @taxId,
      currentOutstanding = @currentOutstanding,
      riskLevel = @riskLevel
  `);
  stmt.run(business);
}
```

**Key Learnings**:
- **`ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE`** is an **UPSERT** pattern — if a record with the same `id` already exists, it updates instead of crashing. This means you can run the ingestion pipeline multiple times safely.
- **`@id`, `@name`** etc. are **named parameters** in `better-sqlite3`. When you pass an object like `{ id: "gst:xxx", name: "Krishna" }`, the library automatically maps object keys to the `@key` placeholders.
- **`db.prepare()`** creates a **prepared statement** — the SQL is compiled once and can be executed many times efficiently.

#### `findBusinessById()` — Lookup by ID

```typescript
export function findBusinessById(id: string): BusinessEntity | undefined {
  const stmt = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM businesses WHERE id = ?');
  return stmt.get(id) as BusinessEntity | undefined;
}
```

