### 10. [`src/ingest.ts`](file:///c:/Users/ASUS/my-agentic-cdp/src/ingest.ts) — ⭐ The Main Pipeline Orchestrator

This is the **conductor** that ties everything together. Run with: `npx tsx src/ingest.ts`

```typescript
// STEP 1 — Parse party_master.xls → BusinessEntity[]
const partyBuffer = fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(process.cwd(), 'data/party_master.xls'));
const partyWorkbook = XLSX.read(partyBuffer);
const partySheet = partyWorkbook.Sheets[partyWorkbook.SheetNames[0]!];
const rawPartyRows: any[] = XLSX.utils.sheet_to_json(partySheet!);
const allBusinesses: BusinessEntity[] = rawPartyRows.map(mapPartyMasterRow);
// → Every row is now a clean BusinessEntity with canonical ID

// STEP 2 — Parse outstanding_legder.xls → raw rows
const outBuffer = fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(process.cwd(), 'data/outstanding_legder.xls'));
const outWorkbook = XLSX.read(outBuffer);
const outSheet = outWorkbook.Sheets[outWorkbook.SheetNames[0]!];
const rawOutstandingRows: any[] = XLSX.utils.sheet_to_json(outSheet!);

// STEP 3 — For each outstanding row: resolve → enrich → save
let foundCount = 0, ambiguousCount = 0, notFoundCount = 0;

for (const row of rawOutstandingRows) {
    const description = String(row.Description || '').trim();
    if (!description || description === 'TOTAL') continue;  // Skip blank rows and summary rows

    const total = parseFloat(String(row.Total || '0').trim()) || 0;

    const result = resolveBusiness({ description }, allBusinesses);

    if (result.status === 'FOUND') {
        foundCount++;
        result.business.currentOutstanding = total;           // Enrich with amount
        result.business.riskLevel = computeRiskLevel(total);  // Enrich with risk level
        saveBusiness(result.business);                         // Persist to SQLite
    } else if (result.status === 'AMBIGUOUS') {
        ambiguousCount++;   // Multiple matches — can't decide, skip
    } else {
        notFoundCount++;    // No match at all — skip
    }
}

console.log(`Done. FOUND=${foundCount} AMBIGUOUS=${ambiguousCount} NOT_FOUND=${notFoundCount}`);
```

**Key Learnings**:
- `description === 'TOTAL'` filters out **summary/total rows** that Tally adds at the bottom of reports.
- Only `FOUND` results get saved — `AMBIGUOUS` and `NOT_FOUND` are silently skipped (a potential area for future improvement: logging these for manual review).
- The `result.business` is **mutated in place** — `currentOutstanding` and `riskLevel` are added to the same object that was in the `allBusinesses` array. This works because objects are passed by reference in JavaScript.

